2026-05-18T22:26:44.5967136Z pybind11 provides CMake targets. There are two modes provided; classic, which is built on the old Python
2026-05-18T22:26:44.5967684Z discovery packages in CMake, or the new FindPython mode, which uses FindPython
2026-05-18T22:26:44.5967992Z from 3.12+ forward (3.15+ _highly_ recommended).
2026-05-18T22:26:44.5968152Z 
2026-05-18T22:26:44.5968219Z New FindPython mode:
2026-05-18T22:26:44.5968328Z 
2026-05-18T22:26:44.5968436Z     find_package(Python COMPONENTS Interpreter Development)
2026-05-18T22:26:44.5968679Z     find_package(pybind11 CONFIG)
2026-05-18T22:26:44.5968796Z 
2026-05-18T22:26:44.5968856Z     # pybind11 method:
2026-05-18T22:26:44.5969034Z     pybind11_add_module(MyModule1 src1.cpp)
2026-05-18T22:26:44.5969170Z 
2026-05-18T22:26:44.5969237Z     # Python method:
2026-05-18T22:26:44.5969400Z     Python_add_library(MyModule2 src2.cpp)
2026-05-18T22:26:44.5969631Z     target_link_libraries(MyModule2 pybind11::headers)
2026-05-18T22:26:44.5969876Z     set_target_properties(MyModule2 PROPERTIES
2026-05-18T22:26:44.5970093Z         INTERPROCEDURAL_OPTIMIZATION ON
2026-05-18T22:26:44.5970292Z         CXX_VISIBILITY_PRESET ON
2026-05-18T22:26:44.5970483Z         VISIBILITY_INLINES_HIDDEN ON
2026-05-18T22:26:44.5970666Z     )
2026-05-18T22:26:44.5970736Z 
2026-05-18T22:26:44.5970811Z For more information see here:
2026-05-18T22:26:44.5971210Z     https://pybind11.readthedocs.io/en/latest/compiling.html#building-with-cmake
